    "updated_at": "2026-10-20T16:20:15Z",
    "body": "The `Path` param type is intended for local paths only. Maybe we should make that more clear. The `path_type` arg is purely for migrating to use `Path` instead of `str`. We couldn't change the default without breaking, but everyone wanted the new `Path` type instead of the old `os.path` strings. But there's a deep assumption that we're working with local paths, so it's fine to use `os.path` internally. Changing that would mean adding a different code path based on what the type was, which is a lot of complexity.\n\nIn retrospect, I would never have added `path_type`, I would have made a new `Pathlib` param type. Similarly, you should probably create a `CloudPath` param type to do exactly what you need.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
